    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, both posting elite efficiency scores. **Gunnar Henderson** (82.77) benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Tong, where a 14% boost in SP skill and a positive platoon edge create an ideal high-floor, high-ceiling scenario. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (79.09) remains a must-start despite facing a left-handed arm; his superior SP skill adjustment against Lodolo highlights his ability to transcend platoon disadvantages. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) is a sneaky candidate for the top performance of the day, as a massive 14% park factor combined with an exploitable matchup against Sugano makes him our most efficient overall play relative to his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas**, both of whom are navigating sub-3.00 xERA matchups against Williams. While **Sam Antonacci** (44.04) narrowly edges out **Miguel Vargas** (40.14) due to his leadoff spot, both are operating in the \"marginal\" territory. **Wade Meckler** (44.10) sits in a similar tier, heavily suppressed by a same-handed matchup against Anderson and a bottom-of-the-order assignment. We continue to monitor the status of our deep injury ward, as the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** forces us to lean on these depth pieces. We have significant reserves in **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Henry Bolte**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** ready to pivot if late-breaking lineup news shifts the efficiency landscape. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **Coby Mayo** (51.81). While he clears the marginal threshold, his negative platoon split against Tong suggests he is the most likely candidate for an early hook if we need to pinch-hit for defensive security or a late-inning stolen base boost. We are currently leaning on the power upside of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.50) and the steady production of **Drake Baldwin** (66.14) to maintain our category standings. With no specific weather alerts, the focus remains entirely on exploiting the favorable park factors for **Jackson Merrill** and ensuring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.66) continues his high-efficiency output from the four-hole against Kremer.",
